<article class="env-remark" id="0487">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0487">Remark <span data-tag="0487">7.3.7.12</span>.</a> In the situation of Lemma <a data-tag="0485" href="/tag/0485">7.3.7.10</a>, suppose we are given an inner anodyne morphism of simplicial sets $A \hookrightarrow B$. Then every diagram $K^{\triangleright } \star A \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ can be extended to a morphism $K^{\triangleright } \star B \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, so that condition $(\ast _ A)$ is satisfied if and only if condition $(\ast _ B)$ is satisfied. Consequently, to show that every object of $\operatorname{Fun}'_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}( K^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ is a $V$-colimit diagram, it suffices to verify condition $(\ast _{A})$ in the special case where $A$ is an $\infty $-category (see Corollary <a data-tag="01BQ" href="/tag/01BQ">4.1.3.3</a>). </p>
